1
00:00:00,567 --> 00:00:03,487
(Leonard:)Good luck catching a man
with that attitude.

2
00:00:05,072 --> 00:00:09,912
(Sheldon:)Boy, oh, boy, this vacation
is off to a wonderful start.

3
00:00:10,536 --> 00:00:12,536
(Sheldon:)The smell of formaldehyde.

4
00:00:13,705 --> 00:00:15,835
(Sheldon:)The whir of the centrifuge.

5
00:00:16,041 --> 00:00:20,041
(Sheldon:)The distant chatter of lab animals
being dispatched for dissection.

6
00:00:20,379 --> 00:00:24,719
(Sheldon:)Mm, I can already feel my cares
just meIting away.

7
00:00:24,925 --> 00:00:27,555
(Amy:)I'm excited to work with my boyfriend.
It's romantic.

8
00:00:27,761 --> 00:00:30,221
(Sheldon:)Way to kill the mood.

9
00:00:31,056 --> 00:00:34,436
(Amy:)Come on, Sheldon. We can be like
Marie Curie and her husband, Pierre...

10
00:00:34,643 --> 00:00:36,853
(Amy:)...who spent their days
working side by side...

11
00:00:37,062 --> 00:00:40,352
(Amy:)...bathed in the glow of their love
and the radium that uItimately killed her.

12
00:00:41,608 --> 00:00:45,278
(Amy:)Screw Beauty and the Beast,
that's the love story Disney should tell.

13
00:00:45,988 --> 00:00:48,238
(Sheldon:)Okay. What do we start with?

14
00:00:48,448 --> 00:00:52,038
Maybe, uh, splicing some genes.
Clone a sheep.

15
00:00:52,244 --> 00:00:55,374
Perhaps, uh, grow a human ear
on a mouse's back?

16
00:00:55,581 --> 00:00:59,021
"Ha, ha! I'm a freak."

